Good catch — right now `isReceived` only checks the sender, so it would also match messages between the *selected profile* and some other user (not you). You need to also confirm the message's `ReceiverId` is **your own** RegisterID, not just that it came from `selectedProfile.Email`.

The problem is the current component doesn't have your own `RegisterID` in scope — it only knows `currentUserEmail`. Add a `currentUserId` state, capture it in `checkMembership` (which already looks up your record), and pass it down.

### 1. In `Intrest` — add state and store your RegisterID

```jsx
const [isPremium, setIsPremium] = useState(false);
const [currentUserId, setCurrentUserId] = useState(null); // NEW
const [checkingMembership, setCheckingMembership] = useState(true);
```

### 2. Inside `checkMembership`, after finding `currentUser`

```jsx
const currentUser = allProfiles.find(
    (user) =>
        user.Email?.toLowerCase() ===
        currentUserEmail.toLowerCase()
);

if (!currentUser) {
    console.warn("Current user profile not found");
    setIsPremium(false);
    setProfiles([]);
    setFilteredProfiles([]);
    return;
}

setCurrentUserId(currentUser.RegisterID); // NEW

const premium =
    String(currentUser.Member || "")
        .trim()
        .toLowerCase() === "premium";
```

